WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:04.540
Ladies and gentlemen, here is one of America's favorite clowns,

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:07.040
certainly mine, Mr. Red Skel...

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:02.140
Red Stoutard.

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:06.410
Ladies and gentlemen, I really feel good tonight.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:08.810
I guess by now everybody sort of knows

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:10.930
that Little Red and I are grandparents.

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:18.730
Valentina and her husband Carlos

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:21.170
gave us a little girl, 8 pounds, 4 ounces,

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:23.010
and her name is Sabrina,

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:24.830
and this is my fraternity pin.

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:28.780
It's kind of exciting.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:30.000
I walked into the hospital and...

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.880
the nurse says, what can I do for you? I says, I'm Red Skelton. She says, it's too late to do anything

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:39.840
about that. Hey, Walter Brennan's on, Walter Brennan's on the show, and he told me about when

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.920
he became a grandfather, he says, the doctor said to him, why don't you calm down, go in the room

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:48.060
there and lay down. So he goes in and comes back, he's out in the hall, and the doctor says, I thought

00:01:48.060 --> 00:02:00.000
I told you to go lay down on a bed in there. He says, I did, but every time I do, they come and take me down to the morgue. But I really

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:03.790
got nervous and excited, you know. The night before when they told me that Valentina was

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:07.110
going to the hospital, I was so nervous that I put my pants to bed and I hung over the

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:18.820
chair all night. Just think, though, me a grandfather and at my age. I'm not far from

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:25.700
50, you know. Only nine years ago. Hey, Gertrude and Heathcliff, the two seagulls were talking

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:29.800
to Sam the stork. And he says, uh, Sam, what have you been doing?

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:37.050
And the stork says, "Oh, just kidding around."

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:41.740
He says, "I delivered another kid to a guy that has 26 kids and he hates his wife."

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:46.460
He says, "26 kids and he hates his wife? Why they have so many kids?"

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:53.130
He says he hopes to lose her in the crowd.

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:57.870
You know, I've been trying to find a definition for grandfather and grandmother,

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:00.000
and all it says in the dictionaries is,

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.740
that they are parents of a son or a daughter who has given birth to a child.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:12.510
Well, I think a momentous occasion like that sort of deserves a more eloquent definition.

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:20.680
Sort of, uh, grandfathers, grandmothers.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:27.340
A gentle title that builds an imaginary wall around the harshness of two words.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:29.030
Old age.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:34.970
The enemy of youth, for we have learned that age is cruel.

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:40.170
Yet regardless to how young you are, how young you think you are, or try to be,

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:45.970
age steps in, unannounced, introduced by your closest friends,

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:49.960
sometimes by saying, "Remember when?"

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:55.890
It's then that we hope that we'll have some brilliance that will blind the observer,

00:03:55.890 --> 00:04:00.000
or cast a shadow over our actions and keep them into semi-darkness.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.830
darkness and we close our ears

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:11.630
So we will not hear the sounds made by progress that knows no sentiment or to hear the song that is sung by youth called

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:15.070
senility

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:16.800
grandmother

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:24.270
grandfather a noble symbol of age a real elegance that's filled with proud moments a

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:30.000
Chance to relive your childhood through the eyes of your children's children

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:41.130
children, grandfather, grandmother, a privilege granted by God to teach the little newcomer

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:49.830
the shortcuts and the ways to face the angry, sorrowful old world, a chance to teach independence

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:59.800
and respect without the aid of groups or causes, a chance to show how to build and not to destroy

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:08.170
A chance to see the innocence of life again, to let our minds romp freely and not notice

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:15.740
the hypocrisy or the puritanical taboos that this little fella doesn't know yet.

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:22.380
A chance to teach and recapture wasted, unimportant seconds of our childhood.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:30.000
To explain youth to that always ambitious youth that sometimes forgets to realize the

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:35.540
importance of childhood they're always pretending that they're a little older

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:41.820
than their bodies are there reasons an intelligent just enough to be well

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:50.550
misinformed ignorant to discipline which teach the true essence of freedom to

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:59.410
teach them to grow into their wisdom far beyond their years grandfather grandmother

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:06.830
a blessed honor a chance to daydream and to notice a bird in flight

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:12.440
and think of an answer for it'll be the first time you've ever been asked why

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:18.640
and to touch a puppy dog and not notice it messing up the place

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:24.370
to see for the first time a bladed grass take on the designs of a cathedral

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:29.800
a chance to see spring in the twilight of our autumn years

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:50.960
"Grandmother, Grandfather, what a new dignity, for now you see love and you feel respect, for now you walk holding two hands, one the hand of tomorrow, the other the hand of eternity."

